CoordSys on non-mesh rprims: curves and points projected from a bound camera

A BasisCurves and a Points prim are projected through the 'map_proj' coordinate
system. The per-rprim rewrite of the material 'space' inputs has to run for every
rprim type: while only HdArnoldMesh performed it, curves and points kept the
authored coordinate-system name, which matches no Arnold camera node, so the
space did not resolve and the projection silently disappeared.

Two copies of </fur> each reference the template, so each has its own projector
camera and its own copy of the material, both coordinate systems being named
'map_proj'. Within one copy the curves and the points share a single material and
a single binding, covering two rprim types resolving one coordinate system. The
copies use the .camera and .NDC spaces.

The projector cameras live inside the template (as in test_13221) so the
coordinate-system camera resolves identically under the legacy scene delegate
(hydra) and the scene index (hydra2).

NOTE: ref/reference.tif still has to be blessed - copy the built
testrender.hydra2.tif once the render has been verified. Until then the harness
finds no reference and the test renders without comparing anything, so it cannot
fail.

See #32 / ARNOLD-13221

author: cyril.pichard

PARAMS: {'scene':'test.usda', 'kick_params':'-c /Cameras/renderCamera'}
